  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ranjeet vs State on 23 January, 2018 Author: Sabina Bench: Sabina High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan Bench At Jaipur S.B. Criminal Revision No. 726 / 2004 Ranjeet, S/o Nanda, B/c Meena, R/o Rajukhera, Ps Chechat, Distt. Kota.",
    "facts": "Appeal filed by the petitioner was dismissed by the Appellate Court vide order dated 23.07.2004. Petitioner is facing criminal proceedings since the year 1991.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner has submitted that as per the prosecution case petitioner was found in possession of adulterated milk. Occurrence in the present case is of the year 1991. Learned counsel has submitted that he does not challenge the conviction of the petitioner as ordered by the courts below but has submitted that the sentence of the petitioner qua (2 of 2) [CRLR-726/2004] imprisonment be reduced to the period already undergone by him. Petitioner is not a previous convict and is the sole bread earner of his family. In support of his arguments, learned counsel has placed reliance on the judgment of this court in Loonaram Vs. The State of Rajasthan WLN (UC) 1977, 571 and on the judgments of the Punjab and Haryana High Court in the case of Bharat Lal Vs. The State of Haryana 1993(2) FAC Cases 65, Mahabir Parashad Vs. The State of Haryana 1993(2) FAC Cases 83 and Anil Kumar Vs. State of Haryana 2015(2) FAC 381. Learned State Counsel has opposed the petition.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner has submitted that as per the prosecution case petitioner was found in possession of adulterated milk. Occurrence in the present case is of the year 1991. Learned counsel has submitted that he does not challenge the conviction of the petitioner as ordered by the courts below but has submitted that the sentence of the petitioner qua (2 of 2) [CRLR-726/2004] imprisonment be reduced to the period already undergone by him. Petitioner is not a previous convict and is the sole bread earner of his family. In support of his arguments, learned counsel has placed reliance on the judgment of this court in Loonaram Vs. The State of Rajasthan WLN (UC) 1977, 571 and on the judgments of the Punjab and Haryana High Court in the case of Bharat Lal Vs. The State of Haryana 1993(2) FAC Cases 65, Mahabir Parashad Vs. The State of Haryana 1993(2) FAC Cases 83 and Anil Kumar Vs. State of Haryana 2015(2) FAC 381.",
    "respondent_arguments": "Learned State Counsel has opposed the petition.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
